"directory. Unset to fall back to home-relative names. ENV: "
"NTASKER_PROJECTS_BASE."
msgstr ""

#: src/ntasker/settings.py:671
msgid ""
"Start directory for a run whose task has no project (or whose project "
"directory does not exist and cannot be created), e.g. '~/Projekte'. Unset"
" falls back to the projects base, then to your home directory -- note "
"that Claude Code refuses to work in the home directory until you answer "
"its trust prompt. ENV: NTASKER_NO_PROJECT_DIR."
msgstr ""

#: src/ntasker/settings.py:678
msgid ""
"Project name (not a directory!) of an optional catch-all project for one-"
"off questions that belong to no project, e.g. 'misc' -- its directory is "
"<projects base>/misc, like for any other project. It gets a fixed sidebar"
" row right under Cross-project, is never grouped or hidden, and its tasks"
" carry no dependencies or directory locks. Unset hides the feature. ENV: "
"NTASKER_MISC_PROJECT."
msgstr ""

#: src/ntasker/settings.py:687
msgid ""
"Start Claude sessions in the misc project without auto memory "
"(CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_AUTO_MEMORY=1), so one-off questions leave no trace "
"in Claude's project memory. Needs a misc project."
msgstr ""

#: src/ntasker/settings.py:692
msgid ""
"Agent new tasks use, and the fallback for any task without one. ENV: "
"NTASKER_DEFAULT_AGENT."
msgstr ""

#: src/ntasker/settings.py:696
msgid ""
"When off, Create + Run and the per-task run button start the session in "
"the background and keep you on the board. Click the running task to open "
"its terminal. ENV: NTASKER_CLAUDE_OPEN_TERMINAL."
msgstr ""

#: src/ntasker/settings.py:701
msgid ""
"How long a live session may stay silent before it counts as waiting for "
"your input (the CLI sends no explicit signal). Shorter reacts faster but "
"flags more false alarms. Default 8 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: src/ntasker/settings.py:706
msgid ""
"Done tasks older than this many days are archived automatically -- they "
"leave the Done column but stay searchable in the archive. 0 keeps "
"everything in Done."
msgstr ""

#: src/ntasker/settings.py:711
msgid ""
"When off, run buttons still queue tasks, but nothing new starts until you"
" press Resume on the queue panel. One task runs per project at a time. "
"ENV: NTASKER_QUEUE_ENABLED."
msgstr ""

#: src/ntasker/settings.py:716
msgid ""
"The inbox: a raw note typed into the topbar (Ctrl+K), `ntasker in` or "
"POST /api/inbox is turned into a task proposal by a single stateless "
"Claude call -- title, prompt, priority, tags and project. You confirm "
"every proposal. Off hides the inbox. ENV: NTASKER_TRIAGE_ENABLED."
msgstr ""

#: src/ntasker/settings.py:722
msgid ""
"Model the inbox triage runs with (passed to `claude -p --model`). Default"
" haiku -- the call reads one note and a catalog of project summaries. "
"ENV: NTASKER_TRIAGE_MODEL."
msgstr ""

#: src/ntasker/settings.py:727
msgid ""
"Let sessions you start in a terminal report themselves, so the board can "
"pick one up and carry on with it. This adds two hooks to your own Claude "
"Code settings file (a backup is kept); switching it off removes them "
"again. Without it, ntasker still finds past sessions of a project but "
"cannot tell which are still running."
msgstr ""

#: src/ntasker/settings.py:734
msgid ""
"Let Claude run ntasker commands without stopping to ask for each one. "
"This adds one allow rule to your own Claude Code settings file (a backup "
"is kept); switching it off removes it again. Without it a session has to "
"ask before it can even report its own task as finished."
msgstr ""

#: src/ntasker/settings.py:740
msgid ""
"A queued task waits while another live session holds one of its "
"directories, and sessions refuse edits inside directories they do not "
"hold. Off: one task per project lane only."
msgstr ""

#: src/ntasker/settings.py:745
msgid ""
"Only start a queued task when every directory it holds has no uncommitted"
" changes. Needs directory locks."
msgstr ""

#: src/ntasker/settings.py:749
msgid ""
"A Quicktask (the prompt in a project's menu, or the agent logo next to "
"it) starts right away: it does not wait for its project lane, directory "
"locks or a clean git state, and does not block them for other tasks while"
" it runs. Off: a Quicktask queues like any other run."
msgstr ""

#: src/ntasker/settings.py:755
msgid ""
"Agents write a Markdown report when they hand a queued run over. Off: the"
" run prompt no longer asks for one (saves tokens) and the report buttons "
"are hidden. Your own run rules are used as they are."
msgstr ""

#: src/ntasker/settings.py:760
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Which sidebar sections are folded -- written by the fold buttons in the "
